0.58.1
- agents.md audit: R12 fixed - all 10 Math.random() call sites now use Math.randInt(n),
  preserving the original distributions. R12 greps clean.
- var eliminated (agents.md 6): 122 declarations became const, 170 became let, none remain.
  Converted with a scope-aware tool that first proved no redeclarations and no reads before
  a declarator in the same scope.
- Removed a redundant Pip.audioStop() before Pip.audioStart(), which stops audio itself.
- Added COMPLIANCE.md recording every R01-R15 result and the reason for each Pip.* write.
- Motorcycle sprites were mirrored: MBL/MBR and RBL/RBR each drew the opposite direction.
  Swapped. Walking sprites were already correct.
- Every identifier inside the modules renamed to readable words; source moved to src/.
- Shipped scripts/ are generated from src/ by tools/build.mjs (terser, mangle and strip only;
  no compression passes, because Espruino does not block-scope let/const).
- Each readable and each shipped module is proved to be an alpha-rename of its input:
  identical AST, identical literals, identifiers in bijection with their bindings.
- On-device JavaScript dropped from 122,934 to 108,095 bytes.

0.58.0
- Rot's Crossing rebuilt in the Sunscar art style; the stretched right-edge artifact is gone.
- The race track is now graded dirt with a packed berm, worn racing ruts and a start/finish
  stripe, instead of a two-pixel outline drawn on the grass.
- Collision for Rot's Crossing regenerated from the new artwork and verified reachable to
  every interaction point and spawn.
- Battle videos repaired: player-side clips were routed at a VIDEO/Granny folder that no
  longer ships, so attacks, faints, victory and defeat silently never played.
- Pause STAT tab reads the live Pip-Boy record instead of a profile argument no caller passed.
- Manifest regenerated from the folder: 12 phantom video entries removed, 37 real assets
  added, including every hotel room background and all motorcycle sprites.
- Modules renamed from single letters to descriptive names; dead C.JS and R.JS removed.
- Rotjaw now uses the bike sprite added in 0.57.0 but never read.
- A finished playthrough's SAV.JSON was shipping inside the tape and is removed.

0.57.0
- Big Iron Hotel main lobby became a hub: Kitchen, Laundry, Boiler Room, Ammo Workshop.
- Penthouse opens after six Scorch Rounds. Motorcycle sprites with the dog in the sidecar.

0.56.0
- Stable non-condensed build. Dogtown collision rebuild, hotel collision pass,
  Sunscar resident low-memory fixes, original full-frame world flow restored.

0.55.0
- Native Pip-Boy Stimpaks, bought from traders and shared with the AID inventory.

0.54.0
- Dedicated low-memory workbench module. Craftable damage buff renamed to Psycho.

0.50.0
- First three-town build: Sunscar, Rot's Crossing and Dogtown Heights, title-screen loadout,
  enemy scaling, the Big Iron Hotel and the six-plate Iron Warden fight.
